## A Threaded Fastener

The previous example involved a trivial extrusion of a complex
polygon, assembled from boolean operations on simple shapes.  This
example showcases the flexibility of the extrusion operation by doing
the reverse.  A simple shape, the basic ISO metric screw thread
profile, is extruded along a helical path to form the threads of a
bolt.  To that is added a cylinder to complete the shaft and a
chamfered hex head.

